  "answer_text": "Because **\"Chase Capital Services\"** can refer to a few different financial entities or services depending on your location and context, the most likely possibilities are outlined below:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Chase Auto Finance / Vehicle Leasing (United States)\nIf you are looking at a car title, lease agreement, or DMV paperwork in the U.S. (especially in states like New York), **Chase Capital Services** is a legal entity name used by **JPMorgan Chase Bank (Chase Auto Finance)**. \n* **Why it is on your paperwork:** When you lease a vehicle through Chase Auto Finance\u2014often for manufacturer partners like Mazda, Subaru, Jaguar, or Land Rover\u2014Chase Capital Services is officially listed as the **lessor (owner)** of the vehicle.\n* **Lease Buyouts:** If you are trying to buy out your lease or transfer your vehicle registration to a new state, you will need to contact **Chase Auto** to get a clean title or a Power of Attorney (POA) to transition the title from \"Chase Capital Services\" into your own name.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chase Capital Services Private Limited (India)\nIf you are referring to an independent corporate entity in India, **Chase Capital Services (P) Ltd** is a financial consultancy firm.\n* **Background:** Founded in 1997 and headquartered in Chandigarh/Mohali, India.\n* **Services:** They offer corporate advisory, debt syndication, securitization services, currency and commodities trading, IPO services, and investment banking. \n\n---\n\n### 3. Other \"Chase Capital\" Entities\n* **Alternative Business Financing:** There is a boutique financier named **Chase Capital** that specializes in alternative business funding solutions like debtor financing, invoice discounting, and term loans.\n* **JPMorgan Chase Capital Trusts:** JPMorgan Chase & Co. has historically utilized trust entities (such as \"Chase Capital XXI\" or \"Chase Capital XXIII\") to issue floating-rate capital securities and trust preferred securities.\n* **FCA Warning Note:** Be aware that the UK's Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) has previously flagged an unauthorized offshore firm operating under the name **\"Chase Capital Online\"** (based in St. Vincent and the Grenadines) for targeting UK consumers without proper regulatory approval.\n\n***\n\n**Which of these are you looking for?** If you need assistance with a car lease buyout, contact information for Chase Bank, or details on a business entity, please let me know!",
